<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panduvasudeva</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Panduvasudeva was, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavamsa">Mahavamsa</a>, the second king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-vijaya">Prince Vijaya</a> who came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> to succeed him. He is said to have ruled from Upatissa Gama and married the Shakya princess Bhaddakaccana, and his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandukabhaya">Pandukabhaya</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a>. Like Vijaya, he belongs to the legendary early part of the chronicle.</p></div>
